 "- Against: the distinction between molecules and distinct functional sequences: many molecules are copies of the same sequence, so distinct sequences ever realised is far below 10^52 (Eden's own 'say 10^40').\n- In support: Eden, p.7, says the 10^52 set 'contains within it all the useful proteins which have existed to date', so Day's paraphrase is a licensed shorthand if 'functional proteins' means 'contained in'.\n- Weaknesses: for D's argument the relevant budget is distinct sequences tested by lineages; neither the molecule count nor 10^40 is that quantity.",
